      "text": "NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 is a family of vision-language models (VLMs) developed by NVIDIA that utilize hybrid architectures, combining Mamba-2, Mixture-of-Experts (MoE), and Transformer layers. These models are designed for multimodal tasks including document understanding, reasoning, and agentic workflows, with specific versions optimized for either maximum intelligence (Super-VL) or local deployment efficiency (Bolt). They represent NVIDIA's effort to provide high-performance, open-weights alternatives for developers needing scalable AI that can handle both text and visual inputs."
