    "summary": "NVIDIA is expanding its open-weights portfolio with the release of the Nemotron 3.5 series, focusing on high-efficiency vision-language models (VLMs). The company has introduced the Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B, a large-scale model designed for complex reasoning, coding, and video understanding with a 1-million token context window. Simultaneously, NVIDIA released the Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B, which utilizes a Mamba-2-Transformer hybrid architecture and 2-bit quantization to enable local execution of agentic tasks within 24GB of memory. To further enhance performance, NVIDIA provided a LiLiCorr speculative-decoding checkpoint for the Bolt model to accelerate token generation. These releases highlight a strategic push toward hybrid architectures and memory-optimized models that balance intelligence with deployment speed for both cloud and local environments.",
